# 🚀 CURLER

[![License: MIT](https://shields.io)](https://opensource.org)
[![Build Status](https://shields.io)]()


Curler is a lightweight script designed to act similar to dirbuster and gobuster but slower and simpler with some added functionality 
### Files

there are two different versions, curler and curler_simple, curler simple has less funcitonality but runs a tiny bit faster
### 🛠️ Built With
* shell scripting

---


## 🏁 Getting Started

Follow these steps to set up the project locally for development and testing.

### Prerequisites
* Hopefully none ??

### Installation
1. download the file or clone the repository

2. add permissions

3. run

---

## 💡 Usage

./curler.sh [url] [arguments]

#   Usage: $0 [-P int ] [-S string] [-D filename] [-B] [-C]"
#      -P parallel mode   [INTEGER]
#      -S suffix mode     [FILENAME OR STRING]
#      -D dictionary mode [FILENAME]
#      -N nested mode     [FILENAME]
#      -R raw mode        [RAW VALUE]
#      -B body mode
#      -C code mode
#      -T title mode
#      -W word mode


# parallel mode (recommended)
runs several operations in parallel threads, amount to be set by the user, if not set defaults to 1

# suffix mode
adds file suffixes to every url ran, can be a single suffix entered as string or multiple from a file

# dictionary mode (recommended )
gets the urls to be searched from entered file

# raw mode
generates all a-Z 0-9 combinations up to x digits determined by the user (do not enter values higher then 4 or 5 as it can take millions of years)

# body mode
runs analysis based on all body text similarity up to 5000 characters

# code mode (recommended)
returns positive to out if code is not 404 (same method as gobuster and dirbuster)

# title mode
runs analysis based on title text similarity up to 5000 characters

# word mode 
runs analysis based on word frequency similarity up to 5000 characters
